+\end{tabular}
+\displaynote{Failure-positive metrics on saved outer predictions. Folds share training data and are not independent experimental replications. No new training or interval estimation was performed.}
+\end{table}
+Fold~3 has 3,051 corrected and 2,820 damaged positive--negative pairs. Its positive AUROC change and negative AP change are consistent because AP weights retrieval positions differently. Pooled AUROC is .779325 for sensors, .777037 after arithmetic omission and .794968 for F2. Fold-dependent score alignment therefore affects pooled metrics without changing within-fold sensor ordering. Setting the visual probability to zero is a particular constant reference, not an identified decomposition of pooled importance. The reduced map retains jointly fitted parameters; it is not a refitted sensor-only comparator.\ev{Audit inputs, source identities and reproducible calculation}{\EvidenceRef{E113}{}, \EvidenceRef{E122}{}}
